{
  "id": "EUVD-2021-13671",
  "enisaUuid": "54fae5e4-e5d1-3645-80dd-d3e1809c931a",
  "description": "An elevation of privilege vulnerability exists in Microsoft Windows when Folder redirection has been enabled via Group Policy. When folder redirection file server is co-located with Terminal server, an attacker who successfully exploited the vulnerability would be able to begin redirecting another user's personal data to a created folder.\nTo exploit the vulnerability, an attacker can create a new folder under the Folder Redirection root path and create a junction on a newly created User folder. When the new user logs in, Folder Redirection would start redirecting to the folder and copying personal data.\nThis elevation of privilege vulnerability can only be addressed by reconfiguring Folder Redirection with Offline files and restricting permissions, and NOT via a security update for affected Windows Servers. See the FAQ section of this CVE for configuration guidance.",
  "datePublished": "Mar 11, 2021, 3:42:16 PM",
  "dateUpdated": "Aug 19, 2026, 4:30:31 PM",
